    "markdown": "# The newest patients in detail {#sec-new-patients}\n\n\nThe newest patients, from Nova 588 to Nova 632, treated exactly like every other patient: each scan is put\nthrough the rule of @sec-the-rule (water peak height ≥ 0\\.35 and water centred at q ≥ 19),\nwithout looking at the labels, most of which are not in yet. Nova 588-595 come from the main archive and Nova 596 onwards\nfrom the scans added on 9 November 2026 (measured 2-6 November), prepared in exactly the same way (@fig-preparation). Of their 265 scans, 52\n(20%) are usable, and **11 of the 45 patients** have both breasts usable.\nMost labels are not in yet; once they are, the patients with both breasts usable can be used to test the comparison of @sec-the-rule\n(@sec-next-steps).\n\n::: {#cell-fig-new-patients .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nCOLUMNS = 8\nrows_needed = int(np.ceil(len(new_novas) / COLUMNS))\nplt.rcParams[\"font.size\"] = 6\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(rows_needed, COLUMNS, figsize=(10, 1.45 * rows_needed + 0.3), sharex=True, sharey=True, squeeze=False)\nfor ax, nova in zip(axes.flat, new_novas):\n    counts = []\n    for side, colour in ((\"LEFT\", \"tab:blue\"), (\"RIGHT\", \"tab:orange\")):\n        _, n_good, n_all, _ = breast_summary(nova, side)\n        counts.append(f\"{side[0]} {n_good}/{n_all}\")\n        for _, curve, _, _, ok in new_records.get((nova, side), []):\n            ax.plot(q, curve, color=colour if ok else \"grey\", lw=0.8 if ok else 0.6, ls=\"-\" if ok else \"--\")\n    ax.hlines(WATER_MIN, *WATER, color=\"black\", lw=2, zorder=5)\n    ax.set_facecolor({\"both\": BOTH_TINT, \"one \": ONE_TINT}.get(outcomes[nova][:4], NONE_TINT))\n    ax.set_title(f\"Nova {nova}: {', '.join(counts)}\", fontsize=6)\n    ax.set(xlim=(2, 25), ylim=(-0.1, 1.8))\nfor ax in axes.flat[len(new_novas):]:\n    ax.axis(\"off\")\nfor ax in axes[-1]:\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"q (nm⁻¹)\")\nfig.tight_layout(pad=0.4)\nplt.show()\nplt.rcParams[\"font.size\"] = 10\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n![Every prepared scan of the newest patients, one panel per patient, tinted by the outcome as in the table (green both breasts usable, orange one, red neither). Usable scans are coloured (left breast blue, right orange), scans the rule rejects are grey and dashed; the black bar is the threshold on the water peak (q 20-22).](new_patients_files/figure-html/fig-new-patients-output-1.png){#fig-new-patients width=973 height=873}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n```{=html}\n<table class=\"table\"><thead><tr><th>Patient</th><th>Labels (L / R)</th><th>Usable scans, L</th><th>Usable scans, R</th><th>Water:Fat, L</th><th>Water:Fat, R</th><th>Outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr style=\"background:#c8e6c9\"><td style=\"background:#c8e6c9; white-space:nowrap; text-align:left\">Nova 588</td><td style=\"background:#c8e6c9; white-space:normal; text-align:left\">NORMAL / CANCER</td><td style=\"background:#c8e6c9; white-space:normal; text-align:center\">2 of 2</td><td style=\"background:#c8e6c9; white-space:normal; text-align:center\">2 of 2</td><td style=\"background:#c8e6c9; white-space:normal; text-align:center\">3.13</td><td style=\"background:#c8e6c9; white-space:normal; text-align:center\">9.08</td><td style=\"background:#c8e6c9; white-space:normal; text-align:center\">both breasts usable: compared</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#ffcdd2\"><td style=\"background:#ffcdd2; white-space:nowrap; text-align:left\">Nova 589</td><td style=\"background:#ffcdd2; white-space:normal; text-align:left\">not yet labelled</td><td style=\"background:#ffcdd2; white-space:normal; text-align:center\">0 of 3</td><td style=\"background:#ffcdd2; white-space:normal; text-align:center\">0 of 3</td><td style=\"background:#ffcdd2; white-space:normal; text-align:center\">–</td><td style=\"background:#ffcdd2; white-space:normal; text-align:center\">–</td><td style=\"background:#ffcdd2; white-space:normal; text-align:center\">neither breast usable: not compared</td></tr><tr style=\"back